+!---- THUNDERSTORM PROJECT FORK: namelist-driven seed for irandp ------!
+! Stock CM1 r21.1 has NO seed knob.  use_truly_random_pert is a
+! `logical, parameter` = .false. (init3d.F ~line 168), so irandp=1 always
+! draws from ONE hardcoded seed and every run produces the IDENTICAL
+! perturbation field -- reproducible, but with zero outcome variation.
+! The loop below is CM1's OWN hook for this, shipped commented-out by
+! the author; this fork does nothing but enable it.
+!
+! Semantics: var7 (namelist &param8 -- an EXISTING CM1 key, so the
+! namelist remains the sole scenario input) advances the PRNG stream by
+! nint(var7)*nk*(ny+2)*(nx+2) draws before the perturbations are drawn.
+! It is a STREAM OFFSET, not a re-seed: different seeds get a shifted
+! reuse of one stream -- decorrelated at every grid point, but not
+! independently drawn.  That is sufficient for "same environment,
+! divergent trajectory", and is upgradeable to a true random_seed(put=)
+! on this same fork if independence is ever required.  The advance
+! stride here deliberately differs from the consumption stride below
+! (which draws twice over 0..nx+2 / 0..ny+2), so no feature aliases.
+!
+! var7 = 0 is a zero-trip loop => bitwise identical to stock CM1.
+! nint() makes a NEGATIVE var7 zero-trip too, which would silently alias
+! to seed 0; pipeline/cm1post/deck.py rejects negative and non-integer
+! seeds so that collision can never reach a deck.
+!----------------------------------------------------------------------!
+        do n=1,nint(var7)
+          if(myid.eq.0) print *,'  pert loop = ',n
+        do k=1,nk
+          do jj = 0,ny+1
+          do ii = 0,nx+1
+            call random_number(rand)
+          enddo
+          enddo
+        enddo
+        enddo
 
